    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0708" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg668"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1611.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 1, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 15th of November, No. 1090. It is accompanied by a printed copy
                    of a supplemental correspondence upon the subject of claims for the depredations
                    of the British cruisers upon unarmed naval commerce of the United States. I
                    await the reply to Lord Russell’s communication which you have promised to make;
                    when a copy of that reply shall have been received, we shall be in possession of
                    the entire argument.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c., London</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
